                    {
                        "form_id": "160f3b24-1efc-466a-a587-c437dc196ebe",
                        "entry_id": "27c3ae3d-e1b1-3780-99b0-00aec0e73e86",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "prepositional"
                        ],
                        "form": "мовето́нах"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "dde6f8bd-0432-3292-b494-4625579c7546",
                        "entry_id": "27c3ae3d-e1b1-3780-99b0-00aec0e73e86",
                        "glosses": [
                            "устар. или ирон. дурной тон; поведение, манеры и поступки, считающиеся неподобающими, неприличными, не принятые в данном обществе; плохой, дурно воспитанный"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "944ffcd9-5649-443b-972e-6f1e8087bce8",
                                "sense_id": "dde6f8bd-0432-3292-b494-4625579c7546",
                                "text": "У нас в Петербурге уж и приказные нынче это за моветон считают."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "76e552ed-8749-4886-8d44-ab79aeabe43c",
                                "sense_id": "dde6f8bd-0432-3292-b494-4625579c7546",
                                "text": "Из под одной дамы моветон Шварцберг выдернул стул."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7f5d998e-b0fc-4552-b386-b217e331925e",
                                "sense_id": "dde6f8bd-0432-3292-b494-4625579c7546",
                                "text": "Хоть это и моветон, но приходится признать, что существует ещё такой способ избавляться от ненужных вещей — дарить их кому-нибудь."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a07b3a85-b9f9-41fc-a18a-bc5da1bfbac7",
                        "source_entry_id": "27c3ae3d-e1b1-3780-99b0-00aec0e73e86",
                        "source_sense_id": "dde6f8bd-0432-3292-b494-4625579c7546",
                        "target_lang_word": "impropriety",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "impropriety",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "87bce44c-e7f8-39de-a8a9-d50bf0ff6da3",
                                        "entry_id": "1b3b38fb-18e4-32bd-953b-627e59abac95",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The condition of being improper."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c5317df4-9d42-47ca-95fc-bcb6fc2f17f2",
                                                "sense_id": "87bce44c-e7f8-39de-a8a9-d50bf0ff6da3",
                                                "text": "If so many ladies of rank wrote books, there could be no impropriety in her following their example,..."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "66811b67-603e-4a2f-9fe4-4d3119654a10",
                                                "sense_id": "87bce44c-e7f8-39de-a8a9-d50bf0ff6da3",
                                                "text": "To see the impropriety of this noninformative prior, note that the posterior results (2.19)–(2.22) can be justified by as [sic] combining the likelihood function with the following ‘prior density’: […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7bc27161-504a-3501-91c0-8d839f86d7db",
                                        "entry_id": "1b3b38fb-18e4-32bd-953b-627e59abac95",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An improper act."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6c6357bc-a8d3-477c-9b4e-0c07f94f6a12",
                                                "sense_id": "7bc27161-504a-3501-91c0-8d839f86d7db",
                                                "text": "Bayh and his supporters ended up maintaining that it was no longer sufficient that a nominee had not engaged in any impropriety; now there must be no \"appearance\" of impropriety. Thus opponents of a nominee could raise an \"appearance\" of impropriety by false charges and thereby defeat him. It was a vicious circle: the nominee would not be condemned for what he had done but for what he had been accused of having done by his detractors."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0176a271-9bbb-3619-811a-6e828e0e898f",
                                        "entry_id": "1b3b38fb-18e4-32bd-953b-627e59abac95",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Improper language."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "51bb56e5-aff6-4bdf-b2b5-6a13222395ab",
                        "source_entry_id": "27c3ae3d-e1b1-3780-99b0-00aec0e73e86",
                        "source_sense_id": "dde6f8bd-0432-3292-b494-4625579c7546",
                        "target_lang_word": "bad manners",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "bad manners",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ed8dc38b-01c6-3e0d-afb6-a5ff8b27f71b",
                                        "entry_id": "5644c25b-1c33-3d4c-8699-9aa5ea8c3a81",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The treatment of other people in an impolite or discourteous way, or incorrect behaviour in public."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "plural",
                                            "plural-only"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "57b2aced-4292-43b5-86e4-96c3de035229",
                                                "sense_id": "ed8dc38b-01c6-3e0d-afb6-a5ff8b27f71b",
                                                "text": "In some cultures, it is considered to be bad manners to talk with your mouth full."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cfbc8ea1-f74d-48be-b936-57107e2c5c9e",
                                                "sense_id": "ed8dc38b-01c6-3e0d-afb6-a5ff8b27f71b",
                                                "text": "We walked out into the sunlight and rode from the church to Rose Hills Memorial Park. My mother was buried in the family plot, alongside my father, my brothers Arthur and Harold, her mother and father, and her sister Elizabeth, who died of cancer. Only one reporter had the bad manners to stick a microphone in my face and ask how I felt. I just walked past him."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
